IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-first-schedule`
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`

-- g1-licensing-duty.l4: Chapter 2 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning
-- Systems Law 5785-2025, s.3 (duty to be licensed) and s.4 (false advertising).  Group G1.
-- Imports prelude, daydate, domain and this group's g1-first-schedule and g1-interpretation.  The Hebrew is copied
-- by script from inputs/law.wiki (src:N is line N); identifiers and glosses are mine and the Hebrew governs.
--
-- Inputs this module takes from other groups, under the plan's standard names (IP = integration point):
--   `licence kinds in force on the day`  (IP1: which licences are in force; G2 with G1's s.10)
--   `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`  (IP2: G7, s.63)
--   `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)`  (IP14: no order is in the sources)
--   `the licensee breached a licence condition`  (IP8: G3, which makes the s.17 training duty a condition)
--   `the licensee is restricted from the work`  (G1's own s.10 record reaches this rule as a flag)
-- An exemption order or an amendment of the First Schedule would be a new vintage of the table, which is not
-- modelled: the Schedule as enacted is the only vintage, and the content of an order is an input.

§ `Chapter 2: Licensing`

§§ `s.3 Duty to be licensed`

-- s.3(a): "No person shall do work on a cooling system as specified in column B of the First Schedule unless he
-- holds a licence of the kind appropriate for work on that system as specified in column A of the First Schedule,
-- and in accordance with the conditions of his licence and the provisions under this Law."  The kind appropriate
-- to the work has two halves: the licence kind must cover the system's capacity (s.2) and the licence kind must be
-- one the First Schedule lists the activity under.
-- src:71 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} לא יבצע אדם עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר כמפורט {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 1|בטור ב׳ בתוספת הראשונה}} אלא אם כן בידו רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע עבודה באותה מערכת כמפורט {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 1|בטור א׳ בתוספת הראשונה}}, ובהתאם לתנאי רישיונו ולהוראות לפי חוק זה.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
@desc What section 3(a) says about one piece of work: it does not apply, or it is permitted, or it is forbidden and why
DECLARE `Outcome of section 3(a)` IS ONE OF
    `section 3(a) does not apply: the act is not work on a cooling system`
    `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system`
    `section 3(a) does not apply: the system is of a class the Minister exempted by order under section 3(b)`
    `the work is permitted: the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, and works within its conditions`
    `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
    `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work`
    `the work is forbidden: the person holds a licence of the appropriate kind but works outside its conditions or the provisions under the Law`

@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
@desc Everything section 3(a) asks about one piece of work: the system, what the act amounts to, the licences the person holds, and the facts about the conditions of the licence
DECLARE `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)` HAS
    `the cooling system worked on` IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system the work was done on; only its cooling capacity in kilowatts is read here
    `the activity the act amounts to` IS A MAYBE `First Schedule activity` @desc The First Schedule activity the act amounts to; NOTHING if it amounts to none of them
    `the limits of the item` IS A `Facts about an act for the limits of First Schedule items` @desc The facts that decide whether the act stays inside the limits of the items that say only
    `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The kinds of the licences the person holds that are in force on the day of the work; a temporary licence is listed as grade 3; empty if the person holds none in force
    `a licence of the person is not in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person holds or held a licence that is not in force on the day (expired, suspended or revoked)
    `the Law has commenced for the work on the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Law has commenced, for work on this system, on the day of the work (section 63)
    `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if an order of the Minister under section 3(b) exempts the class of systems the system belongs to; no such order is in the sources
    `the licensee breached a licence condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person, in doing the work, breached a condition of the licence, the section 17 training duty included
    `the licensee is restricted from the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licence is restricted, under section 10(a) or by a direction under section 10(c), so that the person may not do this work
    `a provision under the Law was breached by the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the work was done in breach of a provision made under the Law

-- Column A, as a decision about the system and the work, whoever does it: the licence kinds appropriate to an activity on a
-- system.  A kind is appropriate if it covers the capacity of the system (s.2) and the First Schedule lists the activity under it.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71); s.2 grade 1, 2 and 3 licences
@export The licence kinds appropriate to an activity on a cooling system, whoever does it: those that cover the capacity of the system (grade 1 up to 18 kW, grade 2 up to 70 kW, grade 3 any) and under which the First Schedule lists the activity
GIVEN activity IS A `First Schedule activity` @desc The First Schedule activity the act amounts to
      system IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system worked on; only its cooling capacity in kilowatts is read
GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`licence kinds appropriate to the activity on the system` activity system MEANS
    filter (GIVEN kind YIELD `s 2 — the licence kind covers the cooling system` kind system)
           (`licence kinds that may do the activity` activity)

-- The licence kinds the person holds, in force, that are appropriate to the system and to one activity: the kind
-- covers the system's capacity (s.2) and the First Schedule lists the activity under it.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
      activity IS A `First Schedule activity`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`s 3(a) — the licence kinds held that are appropriate to the activity` c activity MEANS
    filter (GIVEN kind YIELD `s 2 — the licence kind covers the cooling system` kind (c's `the cooling system worked on`))
           (filter (GIVEN kind YIELD elem kind (`licence kinds that may do the activity` activity))
                   (c's `licence kinds in force on the day`))

-- The same, for the activity the act amounts to.  An act that amounts to no activity has no appropriate kind: the
-- rule that calls this one has already answered that case.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`s 3(a) — the licence kinds held that are appropriate to the work` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the activity the act amounts to`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST activity THEN `s 3(a) — the licence kinds held that are appropriate to the activity` c activity

-- The decision, given whether an exemption by order applies to the work.  The standard rule reads the exemption off
-- the circumstances; the reading that makes the order's own conditions conditions of the exemption passes a different
-- answer in (see s.3(b) below).  The arms are in the order of the questions: is the act work, has the Law
-- commenced, is the system exempt, does the person hold a licence of the appropriate kind, are its conditions kept.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
      `the exemption applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 3(a)`
`the outcome of section 3(a) for the work, given whether the exemption applies` c `the exemption applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT `s 2 — the act is work on a cooling system` (c's `the activity the act amounts to`) (c's `the limits of the item`)
        THEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the act is not work on a cooling system`
        IF   NOT c's `the Law has commenced for the work on the system`
        THEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system`
        IF   `the exemption applies`
        THEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the system is of a class the Minister exempted by order under section 3(b)`
        IF   null (`s 3(a) — the licence kinds held that are appropriate to the work` c) AND null (c's `licence kinds in force on the day`)
        THEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
        IF   null (`s 3(a) — the licence kinds held that are appropriate to the work` c)
        THEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work`
        IF       c's `the licensee breached a licence condition`
              OR c's `the licensee is restricted from the work`
              OR c's `a provision under the Law was breached by the work`
        THEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds a licence of the appropriate kind but works outside its conditions or the provisions under the Law`
        OTHERWISE `the work is permitted: the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, and works within its conditions`

@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
@export The outcome of section 3(a) for one piece of work: whether the act is work on a cooling system, whether the Law has commenced for it, whether the system is exempted by order, and whether the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work and works within its conditions
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)` @desc The facts of the work and of the licences the person holds
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 3(a)`
`the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` c MEANS
    `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work, given whether the exemption applies` c (c's `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)`)

-- The same decision where a licence that is not in force still counts as a licence held: a person whose only
-- licence is suspended, revoked or lapsed holds a licence, but not one of the appropriate kind, so the work falls
-- under Third Schedule item (2) ("no licence of the appropriate kind") and not item (1) ("no licence at all").
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 3(a)`
`the outcome of section 3(a) for the work, a licence that is not in force counting as a licence held` c MEANS
    IF       `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` c
         EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
         AND c's `a licence of the person is not in force`
    THEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work`
    ELSE `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` c

@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
@export True if section 3(a) forbids the work: the person holds no licence, or none of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, or works outside the conditions of the licence or the provisions under the Law
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)` @desc The facts of the work and of the licences the person holds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3(a) forbids the work` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` c
    WHEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the act is not work on a cooling system` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the system is of a class the Minister exempted by order under section 3(b)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the work is permitted: the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, and works within its conditions` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds a licence of the appropriate kind but works outside its conditions or the provisions under the Law` THEN TRUE

-- The prohibition itself, typed by the person and by what is done.  No WITHIN: the section states no period, and a
-- SHANT with a WITHIN sunsets at its deadline.  Where the work is not forbidden the prohibition does not arise.
@desc The acts of Chapter 2 of the Law that are regulated as duties, powers and prohibitions: doing work on a cooling system, advertising oneself as a licensee, and the Minister's powers of s.3(b) and s.3(c)
DECLARE `Act under sections 3 and 4` IS ONE OF
    `do work on a cooling system`
    `advertise oneself as a licensee` HAS `the kind of licence advertised` IS A MAYBE `Licence kind`
    `exempt classes of cooling systems from the licence requirement by order`
    `attach duties or conditions to an exemption by order`
    `amend the First Schedule by order`

@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 3 and 4`
`s 3(a) — the prohibition on work without the appropriate licence` c MEANS
    IF   `section 3(a) forbids the work` c
    THEN PARTY `a person`
         SHANT `do work on a cooling system`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `a person`
               BECAUSE "section 3(a): work on a cooling system listed in column B of the First Schedule was done without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system, or not in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the provisions under the Law"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The interface to Chapter 6 (IP9): which Third Schedule item, if any, the work breached.  Item (1) is work with no
-- licence at all and item (2) is work without a licence of the appropriate kind.  Work outside the conditions of a
-- licence of the appropriate kind breaches s.3(a) but is priced by no row of the Third Schedule (trap T12): NOTHING.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
@export The listed violation, if any, that the work committed under section 3(a): Third Schedule item (1) for work with no licence at all, item (2) for work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work; work outside the conditions of a licence of the right kind breaches section 3(a) and no item prices it
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)` @desc The facts of the work and of the licences the person holds
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`the listed violation committed under section 3(a)` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` c
    WHEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the act is not work on a cooling system` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `section 3(a) does not apply: the system is of a class the Minister exempted by order under section 3(b)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the work is permitted: the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, and works within its conditions` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all` THEN JUST `work with no licence at all`
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work` THEN JUST `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds a licence of the appropriate kind but works outside its conditions or the provisions under the Law` THEN NOTHING

-- The same interface with work outside the conditions of the licence counted as work without a licence of the
-- appropriate kind (item (2)): the reading that gives the breach a sanction row.
@ref s.3(a) (src:71)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`the listed violation committed under section 3(a), work outside the conditions counted as work without the appropriate kind` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` c
    WHEN `the work is forbidden: the person holds a licence of the appropriate kind but works outside its conditions or the provisions under the Law` THEN JUST `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
    OTHERWISE `the listed violation committed under section 3(a)` c

-- s.3(b): the Minister, after consulting the Council, may fix by order classes of cooling systems whose work is
-- exempt from the licence under s.3(a), provided he is satisfied that work on those classes carries no risk to
-- the safety of the public and of those who do the work; and if he fixed an exemption he may fix in the order
-- duties or conditions that apply to a person who works on those classes.  The exemption lifts the s.3(a) licence
-- requirement only: it does not make the person a licensee, so s.4 still binds a person who advertises as one.
-- Whether the order's duties or conditions are conditions of the exemption itself is not said; the exemption
-- is taken to stand (a fork), and the order's duties bind as the order says.
-- src:72 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (א), השר, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, רשאי לקבוע, בצו, סוגים של מערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר, שהמבצע עבודה בהן יהיה פטור מקבלת רישיון לפי אותו סעיף קטן, ובלבד ששוכנע שביצוע עבודות בסוגי המערכות כאמור אינו כרוך בסיכון לבטיחות הציבור ולבטיחותם של העוסקים בביצוע העבודות; קבע השר פטור כאמור, רשאי הוא לקבוע בצו כאמור חובות או תנאים שיחולו על מבצע עבודה בסוגי המערכות שלגביהן ניתן הפטור.
@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
@desc The facts section 3(b) asks before the Minister may exempt classes of systems by order
DECLARE `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` HAS
    `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Minister consulted the Council before making the order
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given (quorum, majority, subcommittee delegation: section 24 to 26)
    `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's opinion: True if the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes of systems carries no risk to the safety of the public and of those who do the work
    `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the order exempts classes of systems from the licence requirement

@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
@export True if section 3(b) lets the Minister exempt classes of cooling systems from the licence by order: the Council was consulted and its advice validly given, and the Minister was satisfied that work on those classes carries no risk to the safety of the public and of those who do the work
GIVEN o IS A `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` @desc The facts of the consultation and of the Minister's satisfaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` o MEANS
        o's `the Council was consulted`
    AND o's `the Council's advice was validly given`
    AND o's `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety`

-- The same power where a consultation counts once the Council was asked, whether or not its advice was validly given.
@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
GIVEN o IS A `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order, a consultation counting once held` o MEANS
        o's `the Council was consulted`
    AND o's `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety`

@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
GIVEN o IS A `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 3 and 4`
`s 3(b) — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` o MEANS
    IF   `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` o
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `exempt classes of cooling systems from the licence requirement by order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
@export True if section 3(b) lets the Minister fix duties or conditions in the order for the classes of systems he exempted: he determined an exemption
GIVEN o IS A `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` @desc The facts of the consultation and of the Minister's satisfaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may attach duties or conditions to the exemption` o MEANS
        `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` o
    AND o's `the Minister determined an exemption by the order`

@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
GIVEN o IS A `Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 3 and 4`
`s 3(b) — the Minister may attach duties or conditions to the exemption` o MEANS
    IF   `the Minister may attach duties or conditions to the exemption` o
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `attach duties or conditions to an exemption by order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The exemption under reading 2: the duties or conditions of the order are conditions of the exemption itself, so a
-- person who does not meet them is not exempt and s.3(a) applies to the work.
@ref s.3(b) (src:72)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of work under section 3(a)`
      `the duties or conditions of the exemption order were met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 3(a)`
`the outcome of section 3(a) for the work, the exemption subject to the conditions of the order` c `the duties or conditions of the exemption order were met` MEANS
    `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work, given whether the exemption applies` c
        (c's `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)` AND `the duties or conditions of the exemption order were met`)

-- s.3(c): the Minister, with the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee, may change the First Schedule
-- by order.  The content of an order is an input and none is in the sources (IP14): the Schedule as enacted is the
-- only vintage, and what an order would change is not answerable.
-- src:73 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} השר, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 1|התוספת הראשונה}}.
@ref s.3(c) (src:73)
@export True if section 3(c) lets the Minister change the First Schedule by order: the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order
GIVEN `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may amend the First Schedule by order` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` MEANS
    `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order`

@ref s.3(c) (src:73)
GIVEN `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 3 and 4`
`s 3(c) — the Minister may amend the First Schedule by order` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` MEANS
    IF   `the Minister may amend the First Schedule by order` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `amend the First Schedule by order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s.4 False advertising`

-- s.4: "No person shall advertise himself as a licensee if he has no licence, and no person shall advertise himself
-- as a licensee of a particular kind if he has no licence of that kind."  "Of that kind" is the same kind: a holder
-- of grade 3 who advertises as a grade 2 licensee holds no grade 2 licence (a fork, with the higher grade
-- counting as the alternative).  The section does not say when it commences for an advertisement, which is not
-- work on any system: the Law's commencement (section 63(a)) is stated for work on a system, so the caller
-- supplies the fact (a fork, with two readings below).
-- src:76 | {{ח:ת}} לא יפרסם עצמו אדם כבעל רישיון אם אין בידו רישיון ולא יפרסם עצמו אדם כבעל רישיון מסוג מסוים אם אין בידו רישיון מאותו סוג.
@ref s.4 (src:76)
@desc What section 4 says about one self-description: it does not apply, or it is permitted, or it is forbidden and why
DECLARE `Outcome of section 4` IS ONE OF
    `section 4 does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for the advertisement`
    `section 4 does not apply: the person did not advertise themselves as a licensee`
    `the advertisement is permitted: the person holds a licence, and one of the kind advertised where a kind is stated`
    `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee and holds no licence`
    `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee of a kind they do not hold`

@ref s.4 (src:76)
@desc Everything section 4 asks about one self-description of a person
DECLARE `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4` HAS
    `the person advertised themselves as a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person advertised themselves as a licensee
    `the kind of licence advertised` IS A MAYBE `Licence kind` @desc The kind of licence the person advertised themselves as holding; NOTHING if they advertised themselves as a licensee without naming a kind
    `licence kinds in force on the day` IS A LIST OF `Licence kind` @desc The kinds of the licences the person holds that are in force on the day of the advertisement; a temporary licence is listed as grade 3
    `a licence of the person is not in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person holds or held a licence that is not in force on the day (expired, suspended or revoked)
    `the Law has commenced for the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if section 4 binds on the day of the advertisement; the sources do not say which limb of section 63(a) governs an advertisement

-- The kind advertised, if one was stated, is not one of the kinds in force (the same kind).
@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind advertised is not among the kinds held` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the kind of licence advertised`
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST kind THEN NOT elem kind (c's `licence kinds in force on the day`)

-- The kind advertised, if one was stated, is not covered by any kind in force (a higher grade counts).
@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the kind advertised is not covered by the kinds held` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the kind of licence advertised`
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST kind THEN NOT any (GIVEN held YIELD `a licence of the kind held is at least the kind advertised` held kind) (c's `licence kinds in force on the day`)

@ref s.4 (src:76)
@export The outcome of section 4 for one self-description: whether the person advertised themselves as a licensee, and whether they hold a licence, and one of the kind advertised
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4` @desc The facts of the advertisement and of the licences the person holds
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 4`
`the outcome of section 4 for the self-description` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT c's `the Law has commenced for the advertisement`
        THEN `section 4 does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for the advertisement`
        IF   NOT c's `the person advertised themselves as a licensee`
        THEN `section 4 does not apply: the person did not advertise themselves as a licensee`
        IF   null (c's `licence kinds in force on the day`)
        THEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee and holds no licence`
        IF   `the kind advertised is not among the kinds held` c
        THEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee of a kind they do not hold`
        OTHERWISE `the advertisement is permitted: the person holds a licence, and one of the kind advertised where a kind is stated`

-- The same decision where a licence of a higher grade counts as a licence of the kind advertised: a holder of
-- grade 3 may advertise as a grade 2 or grade 1 licensee, a holder of grade 2 as a grade 1 licensee.
@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 4`
`the outcome of section 4 for the self-description, a licence of a higher grade counting as the kind advertised` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT c's `the Law has commenced for the advertisement`
        THEN `section 4 does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for the advertisement`
        IF   NOT c's `the person advertised themselves as a licensee`
        THEN `section 4 does not apply: the person did not advertise themselves as a licensee`
        IF   null (c's `licence kinds in force on the day`)
        THEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee and holds no licence`
        IF   `the kind advertised is not covered by the kinds held` c
        THEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee of a kind they do not hold`
        OTHERWISE `the advertisement is permitted: the person holds a licence, and one of the kind advertised where a kind is stated`

@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN held IS A `Licence kind`
      advertised IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a licence of the kind held is at least the kind advertised` held advertised MEANS
    CONSIDER held
    WHEN `grade 3 licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `grade 2 licence` THEN advertised EQUALS `grade 2 licence` OR advertised EQUALS `grade 1 licence`
    WHEN `grade 1 licence` THEN advertised EQUALS `grade 1 licence`

-- The same decision where a licence that is not in force still counts as a licence held (the person holds a
-- licence, but not one of the kind advertised): the advertisement falls under the second limb of s.4.
@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of section 4`
`the outcome of section 4 for the self-description, a licence that is not in force counting as a licence held` c MEANS
    IF       `the outcome of section 4 for the self-description` c
         EQUALS `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee and holds no licence`
         AND c's `a licence of the person is not in force`
    THEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee of a kind they do not hold`
    ELSE `the outcome of section 4 for the self-description` c

@ref s.4 (src:76)
@export True if section 4 forbids the self-description: the person advertised themselves as a licensee while holding no licence, or as a licensee of a kind they do not hold
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4` @desc The facts of the advertisement and of the licences the person holds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4 forbids the self-description` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome of section 4 for the self-description` c
    WHEN `section 4 does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for the advertisement` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 4 does not apply: the person did not advertise themselves as a licensee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the advertisement is permitted: the person holds a licence, and one of the kind advertised where a kind is stated` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee and holds no licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the advertisement is forbidden: the person advertised themselves as a licensee of a kind they do not hold` THEN TRUE

@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under sections 3 and 4`
`s 4 — the prohibition on false advertising` c MEANS
    IF   `section 4 forbids the self-description` c
    THEN PARTY `a person`
         SHANT `advertise oneself as a licensee` (c's `the kind of licence advertised`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `a person`
               BECAUSE "section 4: the person advertised themselves as a licensee without a licence, or as a licensee of a kind they do not hold"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The interface to Chapter 6 (IP9): Third Schedule item (3) is advertising as a licensee without a licence, or as
-- one of a kind not held, contrary to s.4.
@ref s.4 (src:76)
@export The listed violation, if any, that the self-description committed under section 4: Third Schedule item (3) where the person advertised themselves as a licensee without a licence or as one of a kind they do not hold
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of a self-description under section 4` @desc The facts of the advertisement and of the licences the person holds
GIVETH A MAYBE `Listed violation`
`the listed violation committed under section 4` c MEANS
    IF   `section 4 forbids the self-description` c
    THEN JUST `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- When does s.4 commence for an advertisement?  s.63(a) states the Law's commencement for work on a system with a
-- listed flammable refrigerant (a)(1) and for work on any other system (a)(2); an advertisement is neither.  Two
-- readings, both callable; the input `the Law has commenced for the advertisement` takes the answer.
@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN `the Law has commenced for work on a system with a listed flammable refrigerant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Law has commenced for work on any other system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 commences for an advertisement as soon as the Law has commenced for any work` `the Law has commenced for work on a system with a listed flammable refrigerant` `the Law has commenced for work on any other system` MEANS
        `the Law has commenced for work on a system with a listed flammable refrigerant`
    OR  `the Law has commenced for work on any other system`

@ref s.4 (src:76)
GIVEN `the Law has commenced for work on a system with a listed flammable refrigerant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Law has commenced for work on any other system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 commences for an advertisement only when the Law has commenced for work on every kind of system` `the Law has commenced for work on a system with a listed flammable refrigerant` `the Law has commenced for work on any other system` MEANS
        `the Law has commenced for work on a system with a listed flammable refrigerant`
    AND `the Law has commenced for work on any other system`
